{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "So Much to Do at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Where to Research? "}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legwork"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the hard tedious work that has to be done in order to achieve something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Have you started doing any legwork for the assignment? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about the research you do."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "get hold of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to obtain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How else are we supposed to get hold of some information then?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the scoop "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information; news"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've been frantically trying to get the scoop online!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "accessible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easy to obtain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There isn't much accessible information online. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to read through "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to read all of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm reading through all the articles."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le12ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le12ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Perfect Infinitive: - ing Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use perfect infinitives in two ways:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. After link verbs like <span class=\"italic\">seem</span> and <span class=\"italic\">appear to</span> refer to a previous time period.<br/> 2. After phrases expressing emotions and feelings.<br/><br/>  When you talk about results and time, we can use an <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> form to emphasize that one thing happens before another.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I didn't remember <span class=\"strong\">having met</span> her before.<br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Having</span> finally <span class=\"strong\">understood</span> what they meant, I began to do my work.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "After having spent hours last night frantically trying to get the scoop online, I went to bed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I just would have preferred to have slept all night rather than reading through all those articles."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Future Continuous: Stative Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Normally, you do not use stative verbs in the continuous tense because they describe states rather than actions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Future Continuous to talk about an unfinished action or event that will be in progress at a time later than now. <br/><br/>  There are some stative verbs you can use in the Future Continuous tense.<br/><br/>  1. When they have an active meaning<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'll be tasting it to see if it is good or not.</span><br/><br/>  2. When they emphasize change or development<br/> <span class=\"italic\">More schools will be including exercise classes as part of their curriculum.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be having a meeting with the author in a few days. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be expecting a reply back today via email or phone telling me which day works for him."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Will I be hearing about this all day?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be feeling much better too after I've had a good night's sleep."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll be thinking about what it could possibly be until he gets back."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write down a list of verbs that change meaning in the Continuous tense. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (12-15 lines) using 4 of these verbs. Use them in the Simple Future tense and the Future Continous tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading it aloud with a partner. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify verbs that refer to a state."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use verbs which change meaning when used to refer to actions that are unfinished."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice reading aloud a dialogue with my partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le12ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le12ob02re2img05.jpg ", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le12ob02re2img05 .jpg "}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Adam, you're here. You're looking much better this morning.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Hey. Thanks. I'll be feeling much better too after I've had a good night's sleep. Although after having started my research, I don't know when that will be. Have you started doing any legwork for the assignment?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Research? Why would we have to do legwork? Did you do any? There isn't much accessible information about him online.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I tried. You're right but how else are we supposed to get hold of some information then?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le12ob02re2img05.jpg "}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Well, I'll be having a meeting with the author in a few days. I'll be expecting a reply back today via e-mail or phone telling me which day works for him.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: What do you mean? We can do that? You're telling me this now? After having spent hours last night frantically trying to get the scoop online, when I could have gone to bed?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I guess. You also should have checked your messages. I texted you about this.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I didn't get any texts from you! You should have just called me.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'm sorry. Will I be hearing about this all day long?<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: No no. I just would have preferred to have slept all night rather than reading through those articles.", "id": 2, "time": "28000", "image": "engenn10le12ob02re2img06.jpg "}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I said I was sorry Adam.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I know. I'm just giving you a hard time.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: It's okay. Anyway, you must have felt overwhelmed.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I was. On that note, is Boris in today?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: No, he's gone to Chicago.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: He e-mailed me yesterday, said he wanted to speak to me. I'll be thinking about what it could possibly be until he gets back.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'm sure it's nothing major.", "id": 3, "time": "64000", "image": "engenn10le12ob02re2img07.jpg "}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [],